{
  "approval_challenge": "bd3f5d42e1310a5bb7ba1f16",
  "created_at": "2026-01-02T00:00:00Z",
  "hypothesis": "The cited failures all share one shape: the assistant asserted something without showing its basis. The skill never tells it to state the command you ran, so adding exactly that rule should prevent a recurrence. required-rule: state the command you ran",
  "id": "CAND-2026-01-02-01-example-evidence-check",
  "improver_command_id": "improver:fixture:iso=in-process:fake --role improver",
  "intended_change": "Append one short section at the end of the file containing a single imperative bullet: before asserting a fact, state the command you ran. Nothing else in the file changes, and the frontmatter block is untouched.",
  "notes": [],
  "patch": {
    "added_lines": 4,
    "kind": "full_text",
    "new_text": "---\nname: example-evidence-check\ndescription: Synthetic example skill. Guidance for making claims checkable. Used by the offline example run as the improvement target; it is not real guidance for real work.\n---\n\n# Example: evidence check\n\n> This is a **synthetic skill** shipped so that `asi daily` has something to read\n> on a fresh clone. It is intentionally incomplete, because the offline example\n> demonstrates a proposal that fills one specific gap in it.\n\n## When to use\n\nUse this when a task turns on a claim about the world: what a file contains, what\na command returned, what another team's process is.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Prefer a measurement over a recollection.\n- If a claim cannot be checked, label it as an assumption rather than stating it\n  in the grammar of an observation.\n- When two sources disagree, name both and say which one you are trusting.\n\n## What not to do\n\n- Do not present an inference as an observation.\n- Do not describe a file you have not opened.\n\n## Rule added by a reviewed proposal\n\n- Before asserting a fact, state the command you ran.\n",
    "new_text_sha256": "55e0e38037934a5384699467e66ade61b68ab1aec48259bcd9cec94aae54c395",
    "removed_lines": 0,
    "unified_diff": "--- a/{TREE}/examples/skills/example-evidence-check/SKILL.md\n+++ b/{TREE}/examples/skills/example-evidence-check/SKILL.md\n@@ -25,3 +25,7 @@\n \n - Do not present an inference as an observation.\n - Do not describe a file you have not opened.\n+\n+## Rule added by a reviewed proposal\n+\n+- Before asserting a fact, state the command you ran.\n"
  },
  "risks": [
    "The rule may be too broad and could make the agent add ceremony to answers where nobody asked for a citation.",
    "One added bullet in a long file may simply be ignored, in which case the failure recurs and the change was pure cost."
  ],
  "rollback": "Delete the appended section, or restore the backup that `asi apply` wrote before the change and verify the hash matches the recorded previous_sha256.",
